      "title": "Congress stages protest in Kalaburagi demanding CEC Gyanesh Kumar’s resignation",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/congress-stages-protest-in-kalaburagi-demanding-cec-gyanesh-kumars-resignation/article71519999.ece",
      "description": "The Kalaburagi district unit of the Congress on Monday staged a protest outside the Deputy Commissioner’s office here, demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, alleging that the Election Commission was functioning with clear political bias",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-09-28T18:17:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "CJP will not back down till CEC Gyanesh Kumar resigns, says Ranka",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/cjp-will-not-back-down-till-cec-gyanesh-kumar-resigns-says-ranka-126092800707_1.html",
      "description": "CJP spokesperson Ashutosh Ranka on Monday asserted that the outfit would not back down from its demand for the resignation of CEC Gyanesh Kumar over the alleged exclusion of 13 crore names from electoral rolls and challenged him to clear the allegations against him before the press and the public.\nRanka claimed that the Chief Election Commissioner (CEC) had \"defrauded\" 13 crore people by removing their names from electoral rolls and questioned why the BJP was \"defending\" Kumar over the allegations.\n\"For 48 hours, the ball was in Kumar's court; now it is in CJP's court. We will start our nationwide protest on October 2, and we won't back down till he resigns. CJP is a platform which, if it gets involved in any matter, doesn't let go of it until we win,\" Ranka told reporters here.\nOn September 24, the CJP demanded Kumar's resignation for allegedly \"undermining\" voter rights and warned of a nationwide agitation, including \"Jantar Mantar 2.0\", if he did not step down within 48 ...",
